{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-11T05:04:06.110Z","author":"codex-attestation","op":"merge_reconcile","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/comments/2/text","value":"Reuse PR175 canonical identity validation, host exclusion, equivalent-worktree deduplication and conflicting-metadata failures with its real filesystem/worktree regressions. Baseline focused catalog suite reproduced four failures; added PR175 regressions fail against the original discovery and built catalog. Attribution and superseding PR relationship will be documented."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/comments/2/created_at","value":"2026-10-10T03:15:14.820Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/comments/1/text","value":"Release-check reproduction from a worktree: catalog discovery treats sibling worktree directory names as extension package identities, including copies of the pm-web host. Three catalog tests fail. An explicit canonical fleet root removes the invented worktree identities but also exposes the separately tracked missing pm-jev catalog/snapshot entry. No catalog implementation or snapshot was changed in the attestation task."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/comments/1/created_at","value":"2026-10-07T21:10:38.032Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/comments/0/text","value":"The npm release gate for the graph-export feature reproduced three catalog failures in the package worktree. Inventory treated sibling feature-worktree directory names, including the pm-web host worktree, as installable package identities and disagreed with the committed fleet snapshot. The catalog, fleet reader and catalog tests are byte-unchanged from the base; retain this separate existing follow-up instead of changing inventory or snapshots in the graph feature."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/comments/0/created_at","value":"2026-10-07T20:26:19.928Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-10T04:07:54.182Z","author":"codex-sol","text":"Verification receipt is 